From 3d6eafd484b3ac5eb39c1d4e3b08c72c3407b08d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:18:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 39/46] Autoroute tool: dock it at the left; fixes from testing

The Autoroute tool is now a panel that lives in a dialog or docked in the
board editor's left panel column (in place of the Properties panel while
it is shown, the full height of the window).  Docked, a run locks the
editor itself: canvas clicks and keys, menus, toolbars, other panels, the
IPC API and the MCP board tools, until its result is kept or discarded,
and the editor cannot be closed meanwhile.

Fixes found while testing: the tool's destructor touched a frame being
destroyed (crash when a project was switched with the tool open);
kicad_open_project now refuses while a modal dialog is open; screenshots
draw message boxes centred, where Android shows them; progress parsing
follows KiCadRoutingTools' (N ripped) counters; the router output keeps
showing new lines after the first 400; Freerouting's optimize-only runs
no longer skip the optimizer on unfinished boards.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
